{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And it was told the king of Egypt that the people fled.</b> For 'fleeing' should have been necessary — since at first he sent them away of his own will and now they are fleeing. Furthermore, why did he call them 'the people' twice, and the third time he said 'for we have sent Israel away'? Furthermore, how did his heart fill with resolve to go with six hundred chariots against sixty myriads? And even though it says 'and all the chariots of Egypt,' surely he did not gather them from the entire land of Egypt in an instant, for he did not have that much time; rather, he took them from one city, namely Egypt itself. And even from that city he took only those who feared the word of HaShem, and they were the minority. Rather, it is certain that in every place where 'the people' is mentioned, it speaks of the mixed multitude who went with them from the start in the manner of flight, because they saw the excellence of Israel. And Pharaoh reckoned that now, when they see that Israel is entangled in the land, the mixed multitude will say that HaShem has departed from Israel. And because of this, surely the desire of the mixed multitude is to return to Egypt, except that Israel does not let them. And when they see that we are coming to their aid, they too will rebel against Israel and return to us. And on this Pharaoh relied in pursuing Israel with a mere handful of men. And concerning this it was said, 'And it was told the king of Egypt that the people fled' — not that he sent scouts with them, for this matter is not stated in Scripture, but in his own house it was told to him that 'the people' — that is, the Egyptians — went by way of flight, and he hated them for this. And now, 'and the heart of Pharaoh and his servants was turned toward the people' — his heart turned from hatred to love, for he said: now I need them, for without doubt they will be a help to me when they see that HaShem has departed from Israel. And concerning Israel themselves they said, 'What is this we have done, that we have sent Israel away from serving us.' And accordingly, what is said, 'And it came to pass when Pharaoh sent the people' (Exodus 13:17), was said about the lesser ones among Israel, as is explained in the second way.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:20:03.703104849Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}